  { y:105, name:"Paper invented in China (Cai Lun)", era:1, note:"Paper replaces bamboo and silk for writing in China. It won't reach Europe until ~1100 AD, a 1,000-year delay. One of the great diffusion lags in history." },
  { y:313, name:"Edict of Milan: Christianity legalised", era:1, note:"Emperor Constantine legalises Christianity. Within decades it becomes the state religion. The entire cultural trajectory of Europe pivots here." },
  { y:476, name:"Fall of Western Roman Empire", era:2, note:"The last emperor Romulus Augustulus deposed. The Middle Ages begin in Western Europe. Eastern Rome (Byzantium) continues until 1453." },
  { y:570, name:"Birth of Muhammad", era:2, note:"Islam founded in the 7th century. Within 100 years of Muhammad's death (632), Islam spreads from Spain to Central Asia: the fastest territorial expansion of any religion in history." },
  { y:618, name:"Tang Dynasty begins (China)", era:2, note:"The Tang Dynasty (618–907) is considered a golden age of Chinese civilisation: cosmopolitan, with thriving poetry, art, trade on the Silk Road, and a population of ~50 million." },
  { y:632, name:"Death of Muhammad / Islamic expansion begins", era:2, note:"Within 100 years of Muhammad's death, Arab armies conquer Persia, Egypt, North Africa, Spain, and reach the borders of India and France. The speed is almost without parallel in history." },
