    end: "General Robert E. Lee surrendered to Ulysses S. Grant at Appomattox Court House, Virginia, on April 9, 1865. The remaining Confederate armies surrendered over the following weeks. Five days after Appomattox, Lincoln was assassinated by John Wilkes Booth at Ford's Theatre. The 13th Amendment abolishing slavery was ratified in December 1865. Reconstruction (1865–1877) attempted, and largely failed, to integrate formerly enslaved people into civic life.",
